>   PS-What're statues and figurines good for, anyway?

	Spoiler follows




Statues are excellent for opening chests, beating nymphs with when she
has stolen all your stuff, and best, for chopping open with pickaxes -
sometimes there are spellbooks inside.  Nice.

Figurines, when applied, turn into the type if monster they are in the
shape of.  A blessed or (correct me if I'm wrong) uncursed figurine
will become your pet, whereas a cursed figurine-generated monster will
attack you.  This brings up something neat - got a wish?  Wish for a
blessed figurine of a balrog, or red dragon, or marilith, or vampire
lord, etc.

On the subject of robbing priests (Stimpy's spoiler), a better way is
to lock yourself in a room with a pile of rocks, kick the rocks
around, cursed-scroll genocide leprochans, immediately blessed-scroll
tame them, then let them pick up the rocks, and drop gold each time
they drop one.  Pick up the gold, and as Paul Waterman says, You're
Rich!



